From: Personal OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Add firewalld's iptables fix to Dakota's GNOME patch queue

Dakota owns our GNOME junction, so carry the fix as one more patch in its
gnome-build-meta queue. The queued patch explains the change itself.

diff --git a/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-firewalld-iptables.patch b/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-firewalld-iptables.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..477ad12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-firewalld-iptables.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Upstream-Status: Pending
+Exit: Drop when gnome-build-meta adds iptables to firewalld itself.
+Subject: firewalld: discover iptables during configuration
+
+Docker uses firewalld's direct API even when firewalld uses nftables.
+Without iptables in the build sandbox, configure records /bin/false for
+its IPv4/IPv6 commands. Keep iptables available at build time and runtime.
+
+diff --git a/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst b/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
+index 4018dfb6..674db542 100644
+--- a/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
++++ b/elements/gnomeos-deps/firewalld.bst
+@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ build-depends:
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/libxslt.bst
+ 
+ depends:
++- freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/iptables.bst
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3-nftables.bst
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/python3.bst
+ 
